    <DataNode elementId="AT2G44350-MONOMER" textLabel="citrate synthase (mitochondrial)" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="P20115" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="455" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">The mitochondrial isoform of citrate synthase is an important enzyme in the |FRAME: PWY-5690 TCA cycle|. It can also play a role in producing |FRAME: CIT citrate| for extrusion from the roots where it can help to improve phosphate uptake |CITS: [2491664][10427772]|. Following the original cloning of the cDNA for this gene |CITS: [2491664]|, it was overexpressed in cultured |FRAME: TAX-4039 &lt;i&gt;Daucus carota&lt;/i&gt;| (carrot) cells. Increased citrate synthase activity was observed in cells expressing the citrate synthase gene compared to wild-type cells and cells transformed with a vector control |CITS: [10427772]|. In these experiments, the specific activity of the Arabidopsis enzyme could not be measured separately from the endogenous carrot mitochondrial |FRAME: MONOMER-15824 citrate synthase|. But, in a cell culture expressing a high level of the Arabidopsis cDNA, the citrate synthase activity was 0.24 &amp;mu;mol (mg protein)&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; min&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; compared to 0.12 &amp;mu;mol (mg protein)&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; min&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; in the wild type cells |CITS: [10427772]|. Proteomic experiments in Arabidopsis have demonstrated that this enzyme localizes in the mitochondria as would be expected for a TCA cycle participant |CITS: [10427772][11743115][14671022]|. However there is some evidence that it is associated with the cell wall fraction |CITS: [15157177]| and could possibly be secreted |CITS: [18210371]|. This might have interesting implications for rhizosphere organic acid excretion and phosphate uptake.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G44350-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G44350.2" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="P20115" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-18103" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005739" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G44350.2" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT2G44350" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="17137349" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-MIT-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_2491664" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_10427772" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15157177" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_18210371" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G17130-MONOMER" textLabel="Isocitrate dehydrogenase [NAD] regulatory subunit 2, mitochondrial" type="Protein" groupRef="CPLXQT-51">
      <Xref identifier="AT2G17130-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="455" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The IDH-II gene is predicted to encode a regulatory subunit of the mitochondrially-localized NAD+-dependent isocitrate dehydrogenase |CITS: [LIN04][17468208][14671022]|. &lt;i&gt;idhii&lt;/i&gt; mutants have reduced levels of NAD+-dependent isocitrate dehydrogenase activity |CITS: [LIN04][17468208]|. In addition, IDH-II can functionally complement a yeast &lt;i&gt;idh1 idh 2&lt;/i&gt; NAD+-dependent isocitrate dehydrogenase mutant when co-expressed with an IDH catalytic subunit (|FRAME: AT5G03290| or |FRAME: AT3G09810|) |CITS: [16527867]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G17130-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="IDH-II" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="Isocitric dehydrogenase 2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="NAD(+)-specific ICDH 2" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-4992" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005739" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G17130.1" />
      <Property key="ComponentOf" value="CPLXQT-51" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT2G17130" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="14671022" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-MIT-PL" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT3G09810-MONOMER" textLabel="Isocitrate dehydrogenase [NAD] catalytic subunit 6, mitochondrial" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G09810-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="455" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The IDH-VI gene is predicted to encode a catalytic subunit of the mitochondrially-localized NAD+-dependent isocitrate lyase |CITS:[17468208][14671022][16527867]|. Its ability to functionally complement an &lt;i&gt;idh1 idh2&lt;/i&gt; double mutant from &lt;i&gt;S.cerevisiae&lt;/i&gt; when co-expressed with any of the regulatory subunits (|FRAME: AT4G35260|, |FRAME: AT2G17130|, or |FRAME: AT4G35650|) supports this enzymatic function for IDH-VI |CITS:[16527867]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G09810-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="IDH-VI" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="Isocitric dehydrogenase 6" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="NAD(+)-specific ICDH 6" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-5343" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005739" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G09810.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G09810" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="14671022" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-MIT-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16527867" />
    </DataNode>
