    <DataNode elementId="AT4G35830-MONOMER" textLabel="Aconitate hydratase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G35830-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="535" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">ACO1 is an aconitase that can catalyze the conversion of |FRAME: CIT| to |FRAME: THREO-DS-ISO-CITRATE| through a |FRAME: CIS-ACONITATE| intermediate, based on the phenotype of reduced aconitase activity in an &lt;i&gt;aco1&lt;/i&gt; mutant |CITS: [17013749]|. ACO1 may participate in the TCA cycle and other primary metabolic pathways and it is believed to accumulate in the mitochondria and the cytosol |CITS: [17013749]|. Interestingly, ACO1 can specifically bind to the 5&apos; UTR of |FRAME: AT2G28190|, which encodes a superoxide dismutase, &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; and can affect the levels of |FRAME: AT2G28190| transcript accumulation &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt;. Either through this mechanism or other undiscovered mechanisms, ACO1 appears to play a role in the response to oxidative stress in Arabidopsis thaliana |CITS: [17013749]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G35830-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Aconitase 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="Citrate hydro-lyase 1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33458, RXN-33457, RXN-T9-2104, RXN-5978" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G35830.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT4G35830" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17013749" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G41220-MONOMER" textLabel="Ferredoxin-dependent glutamate synthase 2, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9T0P4" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="535" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">There are two genes in Arabidopsis encoding ferredoxin-dependent glutamate synthase. GLU1 is primarily expressed in the leaves and its expression is induced by light and sucrose, whereas GLU2 is preferentially expressed in roots. Both GLU1 and GLU2 have a chloroplast targetting signal. GLU1 plays a major role in assimilating the large amount of ammonia released from photorespiration and is also involved in primary nitrogen assimilation in leaves. GLU2 may be involved in primary nitrogen assimilation in roots.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G41220-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G41220.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9T0P4" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Fd-GOGAT 2" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-26927" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G41220.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT2G41220" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_9596633" />
    </DataNode>
