    <DataNode elementId="AT4G35650-MONOMER" textLabel="Isocitrate dehydrogenase [NAD] regulatory subunit 3, mitochondrial" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G35650-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="615" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The IDH-III gene encodes a regulatory subunit of the mitochondrially-localized NAD+-dependent isocitrate lyase based on its ability to functionally complement a mutation in the IDH1 gene from &lt;i&gt;S.cerevisiae&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [16527867][14671022]|. Although IDH-III, |FRAME: AT4G35260|, and |FRAME: AT2G17130| are all believed to act as regulatory subunits of the NAD+-dependent isocitrate lyase, IDH-III appears to have the most restricted expression pattern and is found primarily in the pollen |CITS: [16527867]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G35650-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="IDH-III" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="Isocitric dehydrogenase 3" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="NAD(+)-specific ICDH 3" />
